    "summary": "Man’s gown (boubou, tobe), hand-woven from hand-spun cotton dyed in indigo. The body is formed of 50 narrow strips hand-sewn together along the selvedges vertically, while the sleeves are sewn horizontally. At the front is a large pocket. Both the front and the back are extensively embroidered with hand-sewn decoration in white, yellow, pink and light blue European cotton thread, in the shape of more or less symmetrical geometrical patterns of spirals, diamonds and squares.",
